3.What does each of the screens in the app look like\
\
1. The app will run a setup process at the start. This will allow the user to set the weights of the categories and add custom ones if they would like. After this, they would go to the report screen. This would show them all of their houses they have saved. If they don't have any, it would say no houses saved. At the top, there would be a button to add a new house. When clicked, you would be able to add a title and/or address to this new house. Also, you can add notes. From there, there would be all of your categories and you can score them. You can click complete and then it will give you your home score. You can also add photos to the house or the categories. There are two other tabs on the bottom which are the settings tab and the compare tab. The compare tab allows you to pick two houses and compare the categories and Homescore of them. The settings tab will have settings(undecided) and a category settings button. Clicking on this will bring you to a new page where you can change the weight of your categories and add new ones if you would like.\
